  "chunks": [
    {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "text": "The Glossary of Image Descriptors has been created by IP Australia to assist its customers in searching for trade mark images on the Trade Marks Register."
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "text": "The document provides a list of all the terms IP Australia uses to describe images, or parts of images, within a trade mark. The pictures, many of which come from registered trade marks, are used only to demonstrate the meaning of some of the terms."
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "text": "IP Australia recognises the intellectual property rights of the owners of all trade marks used in this document. Any unauthorised use of the images may violate trade mark and copyright laws."
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "text": "Note: items which appear in BOLD are 'top level terms'. This means they cover a number of sub-terms underneath them. For example, if you search for the top level term VEGETABLE, your search will return all hits which contain sub-terms such a CAPSICUM, ONION, LETTUCE etc. A full list of top level terms is available."
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "text": "Alphabetical listing of image descriptors."
        }
      ],
